    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.animate\n\n### Description\n\ngetting similar errors to:\r\n- https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/177#issuecomment-1363753439\r\nand\r\n- https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/177#issuecomment-1363753439\r\n\r\nFor me it happens when [neo-tree](https://github.com/nvim-neo-tree/neo-tree.nvim) and [Aerial](https://github.com/stevearc/aerial.nvim) window are opened and a new file is opened from neo-tree where it result in the Aerial window changing size.\r\n\r\nHere is the full err message\r\n```\r\nError detected while processing WinScrolled Autocommands for \"*\":\r\n\r\nE5108: Error executing lua ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1688: Error executing lua: ....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1701: Cursor position outside buffer\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_win_set_cursor'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1701: in function <....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1688>\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_win_call'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1688: in function 'apply_resize_state'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1632: in function 'start_resize'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1288: in function 'auto_resize'\r\n\t[string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_win_call'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1688: in function 'apply_resize_state'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1632: in function 'start_resize'\r\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.animate/lua/mini/animate.lua:1288: in function 'auto_resize'\r\n\t[string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis happens intermittently though (around 30% at a time), still cannot find a definite situation where it can be reproduced.\r\n\r\nIf not possible to fix, is there any way to ignore the error message instead? Not having animation once in a while is better than having a big chunk of error pushed out.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.8.3\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open file\r\n2. Open neo-tree window\r\n3. Open Aerial window\r\n4. Open a different file from neo-tree which has different Aerial window size\r\n5. try several times until the error pops up\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nno error\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nerror pops out",
